#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "CAP-MIGRATION Migration and decommission"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Moving between platforms or accounts without loss, with a fallback window and two-role sign-off."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: movement · depends on: [CAP-OPERATIONALDB]{1}, [CAP-CLASSIFICATION]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Move to a new platform, account or region without losing data, and retire the old one safely."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Copying loses table history; re-binding storage keeps it. A database move is only as good as its verification. A fallback window and two-role sign-off make a cutover reversible until it is proven ([P13]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "A migration plan listing each dataset as re-bound or rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "A rehearsed database move with a verification report."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "A retirement tool that refuses untagged objects."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Database branches do not survive a dump and restore; recreate them. A deployment unit that declares managed storage takes that storage with it when destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "CAP-MIGRATION.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Lake data is moved by re-binding its storage to the new platform where possible; derived tables are rebuilt by their pipelines rather than copied."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "The migration plan lists each dataset as re-bound or rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "CAP-MIGRATION.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "An operational database moves by a rehearsed sequence: freeze writes, snapshot, dump, restore in one transaction, verify (row counts, per-table content hashes, sequences, policies, grants, migration ledger), repoint, unfreeze.{1}*Example:* Before cutover, a rehearsal restore matches row counts and per-table hashes for every table; the production run must produce the same report."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "The rehearsal and the production run each leave a verification report that matches."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "CAP-MIGRATION.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "After cutover the old platform stays read-only for a fallback window (the reference value is 60 days), with history expiry held, until a restore drill passes on the new one."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Expiry jobs on the old platform are paused for the window; the drill report exists."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "CAP-MIGRATION.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Cutover, rollback and decommission need sign-off from both the Data Lead and the Technical Lead; either may halt."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "The decommission record carries both sign-offs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "CAP-MIGRATION.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "Before any drop or decommission, each object's provenance is proved from first-hand evidence, audit is archived, and an immutable archive exists with a tested retrieval. Deletion is a plain delete, never a forced one."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-migration.md
msgid "The retirement tool refuses objects not tagged simulated or derived; the archive retrieval test has passed."
msgstr ""

